    <string name="events_simulator_helper">Debug fixture only. Timer tests outside-screen arrival. Emit next is immediate. Burst fills enough rows to scroll. Insert older changes list order without changing existing IDs. Remove oldest tests provider-removal candidate advancement.</string>
    <string name="events_simulator_guide_title">Attention test guide</string>
    <string name="events_simulator_guide_body">Reset lab → choose Rotation or Random → Next expectation → open Events. The popup names the scenario, seed, target position, preferred placement, queue counts, and expected button results. Rotation cycles top, middle, bottom, then blocking-freeze. Random is seeded and replayable. If the stated next state does not happen, that is a bug.</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_scenario">Scenario: %1$s</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_mode">Mode: %1$s · seed %2$d · step %3$d</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_target">Target: row %1$d of %2$d · %3$s</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_placement">Placement expectation: prefer %1$s; safe fallback is allowed when geometry cannot fit it.</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_expected_action">Expected press: %1$s</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_blocking">BLOCKING: displayed list is frozen at scenario entry while provider truth may keep advancing. Acknowledge must release the freeze and reveal accumulated provider rows.</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_rotation">Rotation: top+Acknowledge → middle+Later → bottom+Suspend → middle+Suppress → blocking+Acknowledge → repeat.</string>
    <string name="events_attention_lab_random">Random mode is deterministic for the displayed seed; reuse that seed to reproduce the same scenario sequence.</string>
